wing matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix can be obtained from the identity matrix by permuting its columns. Therefore, $A$ is a permutation matrix.\n\nThe inverse of a permutation matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}={P}^{T}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6affd858-749d-5a94-854e-ddadd790ae45" :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Permutation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b22600a-7a48-5100-be68-c1220ab2b46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367636} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5ab357-7cac-5a9d-80af-bda0990c82d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367637} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb9ec44-1520-5b8c-a578-9ecf9cc410db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367638} {:answer/id #uuid "51475dd7-0bce-58ad-aac0-9ae6b923f4c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367639} {:answer/id #uuid "f08b447b-d302-56fc-bdc6-f5bd64bdfa68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51475dd7-0bce-58ad-aac0-9ae6b923f4c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367639} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d7e95b-5b2c-5901-b8fa-c13a69f38649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97bb2745-8331-5ad5-a7c9-9978ce0ea5a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-135367" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix can be obtained from the identity matrix by permuting its columns. Therefore, $A$ is a permutation matrix.\n\nThe inverse of a permutation matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}={P}^{T}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6affd858-749d-5a94-854e-ddadd790ae45" :knowledge-point/title "Inverting a Permutation Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e65ae82-d321-5e1c-9c99-36c2043eabfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367643} {:answer/id #uuid "e944ae64-ddc8-5c0c-9223-92557c569a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367644} {:answer/id #uuid "86